CLAUDE:
Gradio 5.x uses a clean modern API. The ChatInterface in version 5 has a simplified signature 
compared to earlier versions — several parameters that existed in v3/v4 were removed or renamed.

For Gradio 5, the ChatInterface accepts:
- fn (required) — the chat function
- examples — list of example prompts
- type — message format (defaults to "messages" in v5)

Key difference from earlier versions — in Gradio 5 the chat history is passed as a list of 
dictionaries with "role" and "content" keys, rather than tuples of (user_message, bot_response).
This is why the chat_with_finn function needs to handle both formats:
    for exchange in history[-6:]:
        if isinstance(exchange, dict):
            role = "Student" if exchange["role"] == "user" else "Finn"
        elif isinstance(exchange, (list, tuple)) and len(exchange) == 2:
            history_text += f"Student: {exchange[0]}\nFinn: {exchange[1]}\n"
